almanacA0a — CC BY 4.0, for the text, the mathematics and the data
==================================================================

Copyright (c) 2026 Tamás Hausel and the Institute of Science and Technology
Austria (ISTA).

This package contains two kinds of material and they carry two licences.
`LICENSE` beside this file is the MIT licence and covers everything that runs.
THIS file covers everything written to be read. The split is by file, and the
rule is meant to be applied mechanically rather than interpreted: if you can
tell which list a file is in, you know its licence.

WHY TWO FILES RATHER THAN ONE. They were one document until 2026-09-09, which
was accurate and unreadable to a machine: a licence detector cannot match a file
that states two licences, so the repository was published as "Other /
NOASSERTION" — a label that tells a reader less than either licence does. The
canonical MIT text now sits alone in `LICENSE` where a detector can find it, and
this file carries the half that has no standard single-file form. Nothing about
the terms changed in the split.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. TEXT, MATHEMATICS AND DATA — CC BY 4.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything written to be read, and the records that support it:

  edition/paper.pdf, edition/paper.tex          the paper
  edition/source/informal/**                    the signed goal, the proof,
                                                the referee reports, the ledger
  edition/*.html, edition/*.md                  the reader-facing pages and guides
  edition/CONCORDANCE.json, edition/MANIFEST.json, edition/DIST_MANIFEST.json
  edition/sources-cited/**                      the statement cards
  README.md, AGENTS.md, CITATION.cff

Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0). You may share and adapt this material for any purpose, including
commercially, provided you give appropriate credit, link to the licence, and
indicate whether changes were made.

  Licence text:  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
  Summary:       https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  SPDX:          CC-BY-4.0

HOW TO ATTRIBUTE: cite the edition as CITATION.cff specifies. An edition is a
versioned, hash-pinned object; citing it without its version defeats the point
of pinning it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. SOFTWARE — MIT, in `LICENSE`
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything that runs or is compiled:

  edition/*.py                     the assembler, the renderers, the verifier
  edition/palomar/**               the disclosure layer's scripts
  edition/source/lean/**           the Lean 4 sources of the formal layer
  edition/source/julia/**          the computational instrument, where present
  .gitlab-ci.yml                   the publication job

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. WHAT NEITHER LICENCE COVERS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

THIRD-PARTY WORK REMAINS ITS AUTHORS'. The statement cards under
`edition/sources-cited/` are this project's own descriptions of results in the
published literature; they quote briefly and cite in full, and that quotation is
the authors' work, not ours to license. No paper by anyone else is redistributed
in this package — the cards name where each source is held and do not carry it.

TOOLCHAINS ARE NOT REDISTRIBUTED. Lean 4, Mathlib, Julia and their packages carry
their own licences and are named, with pinned versions, in the reproducibility
recipe rather than shipped here.

A LICENCE IS NOT A WARRANT. This file says what you may DO with the material. It
says nothing about what is proved, or how well: that is the concordance's job,
and every claim in this edition carries its own warrant — refereed argument,
computation over a stated range, or a proof-kernel certificate. The three are
kept visibly distinct and a permissive licence does not blur them.
